    "text": "For two thermodynamic process temperature and volume, diagrams are drawn. In the first process, it is a straight line having initial and final coordinates as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, whereas in second process it is a rectangular hyperbola having initial and final coordinates (V<sub>0</sub>, T<sub>0</sub>) and (2V<sub>0</sub>, T<sub>0</sub>/2). Then the ratio of work done in the two processes must be<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0010_54852a17be6d.jpg\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 141px;\" />"
